def unique_in_order(items):
    result = []
    for item in items:
        if not any(item == seen for seen in result):
            result.append(item)
    return result

This preserves first-occurrence order and supports unhashable values such as dictionaries and lists. Equality comparisons must be well-behaved; the straightforward implementation is O(n²) in the number of items.
